        "title": "TS2783 False Positive",
        "body": "TypeScript reports that `id` is specified more than once and will be overwritten when an object literal spreads the result of `find('foo') ?? { label: 'Foo' }`. The spread has type `Thing | { label: string }`, so `id` is not present on every union constituent and is not always overwritten. Expected behavior is no TS2783 diagnostic for a property that is only present in some constituents of the spread union.",
